From eae9165f35ee7a7ef344f3b592d893731693cb83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:54:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] feat(control-plane): add the deployment workflow and the
 runtime launcher contract

Nothing in the control plane could start an inference instance: the
reconciler started an empty workflow and plugins cannot be imported by
the control plane. Add forgemesh.controlplane.deployment:

- RuntimeLauncher, the boundary to a runtime backend: launch a
  LaunchRequest (instance key, tenant, resource, spec, allocation and
  devices) into a LaunchedInstance (instance id, base url, protocol,
  validated like status.endpoints), verify it, stop it by instance id,
  plus an optional prepare step. Each call must be idempotent because
  steps are retried and re-executed after a restart.
- The deployment workflow prepare-model -> launch-instance ->
  verify-instance; DeploymentSteps runs the steps on a launcher and
  registers "stop" as the compensation of launch-instance.
- deployment_run_key(uid): one deployment run (and instance key) per
  resource uid. There is no update flow, so a generation change can
  neither start a second deployment nor hide the first one from delete.
- DeploymentReleaser, a ReleaseProvider that cancels an in-flight run
  with cleanup and stops an instance that may still be running.
- InMemoryLauncher, a test double; real launchers come later.
- workflow_db_path(): the workflow store lives in its own file next to
  the control-plane database so its frequent step writes never wait for
  the registry's write lock.

The package depends on the workflow contract only, not on the workflow
runtime, which the control-plane image does not ship yet.
